{"id":790,"root":"كمل","bw":"kml","tr":"k-m-l","found":true,"html":"<div class=\"lane-entry\">See Supplement </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\">  <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">كَمَلَ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>He,</em> or <em>it, was,</em> or <em>became, perfect;</em> and sometimes, <em>it was,</em> or <em>became, complete, entire, whole,</em> or <em>full;</em> which latter signification is more properly expressed by <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">تَمَّ</span>, which see. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">كَاملٌ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>Complete</em> with respect to bodily vigour, having attained the usual term thereof. See <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لَيثُ عِفِرِّينَ</span>, art. <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عفر</span>. Also <em>Consummate, perfect.</em> </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">عَينُ الكَمَالِ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span>: see <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">فَقَأَ</span>. </div><div class=\"lane-entry\"> <span class=\"lane-form\"> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">مُكَمِّلَاتُ</span> <span class=\"lane-ar\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">*</span> </span> <em>Supererogatory acts of religious service.</em> </div>","pages":null,"shownPages":null,"chars":1002,"entries":5,"shownEntries":5,"truncated":false,"match":"direct","key":"kml"}